  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Immortal Crane Sect disciples describe a shocking event at Tian Ti Mountain: Gu Immortals already surround the mountain while the ten great Central Continent sects send elite disciples to contest under an agreement that the immortals themselves will not strike.",
      "chapters": [
        335
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "loc_tian_ti",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Zheng’s fellow disciples name the same contest as competition among those ten sect elites.",
      "chapters": [
        336
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan, still in Southern Border, reckons that the Central Continent blessed land should have opened by then. He calls the intact inheritance many times better than the three kings inheritance, and notes that only disciples of the ten great sects can enter the Tian Ti Mountain contest.",
      "chapters": [
        337
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "No chapter describes her living body.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hu Immortal land spirit formed from her is like a little girl, with snowy white skin glowing with pinkness, shiny large black eyes, and tiny pink lips. A snow white and pure fox tail grows behind her back, furry and fluffy.",
      "chapters": [
        372
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-spirit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lord Sky Crane tells Fang Zheng that after a Gu Immortal dies, remaining fragments of will and soul mix with the blessed land’s powers to form a land spirit, and that the Hu Immortal land spirit he saw was formed from the former Gu Immortal Bai Hu. Without her past life’s memories, only lingering desires remain. Inside the blessed land she can manipulate heavenly power freely, combat a Gu Immortal, and seal any rank one to five Gu worm at will; only rank six Immortal Gu move freely there. The owner of the blessed land gains her loyalty, yet she cannot leave it; within it she is equal to a Gu Immortal. The true essence of the Hu Immortal Inheritance is that wide and rich blessed land. She appears as a little girl with snow white skin and a snow white fox tail, and she toys with the climbing disciples from the air.",
      "chapters": [
        372
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-spirit-powers",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lord_sky_crane",
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "sys_gu_worms",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "inh_hu_immortal_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hu Immortal was an enslavement path Gu Master who controlled fox groups. During her fifth earthly calamity the blue charm lightning shadow appeared; the fox groups could not stop it, she was forced into close combat, and she lost her life.",
      "chapters": [
        409
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fifth-earthly-calamity",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Little Hu Immortal is formed from the obsession of the female Gu Immortal Fairy Bai Hu.",
      "chapters": [
        650
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dang-hun-palace",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_little_hu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The cave Fang Yuan occupies was dug from the center of Dang Hun Mountain by Fairy Bai Hu, the site where she built Dang Hun Palace. He refuses to restore that former palace because her bedroom was too pink and filled with a feminine aura that does not suit him.",
      "chapters": [
        651
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dang-hun-palace",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_dang_hun_mountain",
        "loc_dang_hun_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is named as an enslavement path lone cultivator of Central Continent who died in that fifth earthly calamity to the blue charm lightning shadow.",
      "chapters": [
        1184
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-restated",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
